# SKILL: Model Base Capability Evaluation Pipeline (Multi-Dimensional Benchmarking)

This document defines the standardized execution protocol and mathematical principles for running the multi-dimensional capability evaluation pipeline. This SKILL bypasses standard Cross-Entropy (CE) loss and provides direct quantitative measurements of the structural advantages of isomorphic (LoRA) vs. heterogeneous (FFT-RoPE/Hybrid) model architectures.

---

## 🌟 1. Core Evaluation Architecture

The evaluation skill evaluates five core capabilities of trained models:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Model Evaluation Skill Pipeline (skill_model_evaluation.py)"] --> B["Dimension 1: Attention Entropy"]
    A --> C["Dimension 2: Representation Isotropy (SVD)"]
    A --> D["Dimension 3: Context Extrapolation (Needle-in-a-Haystack)"]
    A --> E["Dimension 4: Distractor Robustness"]
    A --> F["Dimension 5: Periodic Motif Capture (Genomics)"]

    B --> B1["H(A) = - Σ p * log(p) <br>Lower = Sharper focus"]
    C --> C1["Singular Value Entropy <br>Higher = Uniform representation (No dimensional collapse)"]
    D --> D1["QK Retrieval Ratio up to 8K tokens <br>Higher = Long-range global alignment"]
    E --> E1["Context focus retention under random noise <br>Higher = Resilient to semantic drift"]
    F --> F1["Spectral entropy ratio on periodic inputs <br>Higher = Captures structural periodicity"]
```

---

## 📐 2. The Five Evaluation Dimensions

### Dimension 1: Attention Entropy (專注度與結構化能力)
* **Goal**: Measure how sharply focused the attention mechanism is when routing sequence coordinates.
* **Mathematical Indicator**: Shannon Entropy of the attention weight distribution:
  $$H(A) = - \sum_{j} A_{ij} \log A_{ij}$$
  * **Evaluation Standard**: **Lower entropy = sharper attention focus**. This translates to high efficiency in sequence coordinate tracking and geometrical precision.

### Dimension 2: Representation Isotropy (表徵空間各向同性與防維度崩塌)
* **Goal**: Evaluate the distribution uniformity of token features in the hidden state space to avoid the "Narrow Cone Effect" (維度退化).
* **Mathematical Indicator**: Singular Value Entropy derived from Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) on centered hidden states $X_{centered} = U \Sigma V^T$:
  $$p(\sigma_i) = \frac{\sigma_i}{\sum_k \sigma_k}$$
  $$\text{Isotropy Score} = \frac{-\sum_i p(\sigma_i) \log p(\sigma_i)}{\log D}$$
  * **Evaluation Standard**: **Higher Isotropy Score (closer to 1.0) = richer, more uniform feature representation**. This proves the model uses all latent dimensions effectively and maintains high context capability.

### Dimension 3: Context Length Extrapolation (長文本外推與檢索一致性)
* **Goal**: Test if the model's query-key alignment degrades as context expands (Needle-in-a-Haystack validation).
* **Mathematical Indicator**: Retrieval attention ratio at target lengths (from 128 to 4096+ tokens):
  $$\text{Retrieval Ratio} = \frac{\text{Sum of QK attention on needle tokens}}{\text{Mean attention on distractor tokens}}$$
  * **Evaluation Standard**: **Higher Retrieval Ratio = stronger positional consistency and context extrapolation capacity**.

### Dimension 4: Context Distractor Robustness (抗干擾魯棒性)
* **Goal**: Measure the query-key focus decay when random irrelevant sequences (distractors) are injected.
* **Mathematical Indicator**: Context Retention Index (the sum of query-to-key attention weights after inserting varying amounts of distractors).
  * **Evaluation Standard**: **Higher Retention = stronger alignment resilience against semantic drift**.

### Dimension 5: Periodic Motif Capture (週期性結構特徵捕獲)
* **Goal**: Evaluate how well the model parses periodic structural motifs (e.g. genomic start-stop codons in CPTAC or repeating loop blocks in code).
* **Mathematical Indicator**: Periodic Capture Index (PCI) comparing the Shannon Spectral Entropy of features under repeating inputs vs. random inputs:
  $$\text{PCI} = \frac{\text{Spectral Entropy (Random)}}{\text{Spectral Entropy (Periodic)}}$$
  * **Evaluation Standard**: **Higher PCI = superior discovery of repeating harmonic structures in the sequence domain**.

