## 💻 3. Skill Execution Runbook

The execution engine is fully integrated into the workspace:
👉 **[skill_model_evaluation.py](file:///mnt/home/caijingnina-gmai-11e66a/wisdomCoreV2/task03_CPT_gemma_1b/skill_model_evaluation.py)**

### Step 1: Request a Compute Node via Slurm
We must run evaluations on a GPU-enabled node. Request an interactive shell or submit a lightweight job:
```bash
srun --partition=p03 --nodes=1 --gres=gpu:1 --pty bash
```

### Step 2: Running the Evaluation Script
Execute the script by selecting the targeted architecture configuration and checkpoint path.

#### Option A: Evaluate Pure LoRA (Isomorphic)
```bash
python3 /mnt/home/caijingnina-gmai-11e66a/wisdomCoreV2/task03_CPT_gemma_1b/skill_model_evaluation.py \
  --model lora \
  --checkpoint ~/gemma3_cpt_checkpoints_1K_lora/final_gemma3_cpt_1k_lora.pth \
  --output ~/lora_evaluation_report.json
```

#### Option B: Evaluate Pure FFT-RoPE (Heterogeneous)
```bash
python3 /mnt/home/caijingnina-gmai-11e66a/wisdomCoreV2/task03_CPT_gemma_1b/skill_model_evaluation.py \
  --model fftrope \
  --checkpoint ~/agigemma3_cpt_checkpoints_1K_fftrope/final_agigemma3_cpt_1k_fftrope.pth \
  --output ~/fftrope_evaluation_report.json
```

#### Option C: Evaluate Hybrid Model (LoRA + FFT)
```bash
python3 /mnt/home/caijingnina-gmai-11e66a/wisdomCoreV2/task03_CPT_gemma_1b/skill_model_evaluation.py \
  --model hybrid \
  --checkpoint ~/agigemma3_cpt_checkpoints_1K_lorafftrope/final_agigemma3_cpt_1k_lorafftrope.pth \
  --output ~/hybrid_evaluation_report.json
```

---

## 📊 4. Structural Metrics Interpretation Guide

Use this reference table to evaluate the outputs generated by the skill pipeline:

| Dimension Metric | Target Metric Range | Ideal Behavior (Pure LoRA) | Ideal Behavior (FFT-RoPE) | Expected Winner / Rationale |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Attention Entropy** | $0.0 \sim \log(L)$ | High $\sim$ Mid (diffusion) | **Very Low** (sharp focus) | **FFT-RoPE / Hybrid** <br>Phase-locking acts as an explicit structural anchor, yielding sharp focus. |
| **Isotropy Score** | $0.0 \sim 1.0$ | Low ($0.3 \sim 0.5$) | **Very High** ($0.8 \sim 0.95$) | **FFT-RoPE / Hybrid** <br>Frequency rotation naturally mitigates narrow cone collapsing. |
| **Extrapolation Ratio @ 4K** | $> 10.0$ | Poor ($< 2.0$) | **Excellent** ($> 15.0$) | **FFT-RoPE / Hybrid** <br>Continuous phase coordinates maintain global consistency. |
| **Distractor Robustness** | $0.0 \sim 1.0$ | Moderate decay | **High retention** | **FFT-RoPE / Hybrid** <br>Geometrical coordinates anchor attention from OOD noise. |
| **Periodic Capture (PCI)** | $> 1.0$ | Near $1.0$ (struggles) | **High** ($> 1.5$) | **FFT-RoPE / Hybrid** <br>FFT phase updates specialize in capturing repeating patterns. |

> [!TIP]
> **Why the Hybrid model is highly anticipated:**
> While Pure LoRA converges faster in early-stage CE token loss due to direct weight optimization, the Hybrid configuration combines the semantic fast-path of LoRA (r=4) with the structural stability and length resilience of FFT-RoPE. It is expected to yield the most balanced scores across all 5 dimensions.

---

## 🔧 5. Maintenance & Extensions
* **Adding New Evaluation Data**: Modify the `evaluate_` methods in `skill_model_evaluation.py` to hook new layers or read different token indices.
* **Batch Testing**: You can loop over multiple checkpoint steps to plot a learning curve of *Attention Entropy vs. Training Step*.
